**Definition 1.4 (lawful prefixes and raw exits).** $\Omega_2$ consists of
all acquisition-or-later prefixes of this entrance with canonical source
and service frames and canonical fixed installation words. Never-install
prefixes, every allowed old Ready activation position, and every interior
installation and later service cut are included. Boot and preparation
precede these cuts but remain in their absolute histories and bills.

Unknown object numbers are canonical requests with typed negative results.
An enabled wrong raw IN bit has its actual successor and receipt even if
canonical extendibility fails. These one-edge exits are represented by the
structural rules. They are not illegal `none`. Subsequent arbitrary
noncanonical continuations are outside the inversion/progress assertion.
Complete malformed frames have the finite rejection branches specified in
§6. Unauthorized, busy-second-call and premature unsealed reads execute
nothing. The task domain does not turn such nonexecutions into rejects.

